  "caption": "Quinn has a side gig as a weather forecaster, using one grumpy knee. On cold mornings the knee complained, so Quinn stayed on the couch all winter — and it didn't improve.\n\nLarge studies find only a weak link between weather and joint pain. Memory bias, winter inactivity, mood and sleep often explain much of it, though cold can make tissues feel stiffer.\n\nWhat can help: keep moving through winter with indoor walks or heated-pool sessions, take longer warm-ups on cold days, dress your joints warmly, and look after sleep, mood and routine.\n\nIf pain persists or keeps getting worse, get it assessed — whatever the season.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
